@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.6.0
@changelog
  - Codename: Six Seasons and a Movie
  - Soft-key sets: nine of them, each with a number and a name. Soft-Key Set, engage takes the set number as its parameter, so a set sits on any key, a foot switch or a Stream Deck tile. Sets 8 and 9 are the two Layer 1 coordinates that carry SSL's own channel-strip and bus-comp rows, editable now wherever the plug-in leaves a key free, and added as 8 and 9 rather than renumbering 1 to 7, because bindings point at these numbers.
  - The matrix is the editor: nine rows, six columns. Click a cell to go to that bank on the surface and in the editor, double-click to rename it, right-click for copy, cut and paste of the whole bank, its dynamic kind, your presets and the factory banks.
  - A bank can be named, and the name is announced in the mode-change banner and listed in the focused-track panel. The set comes first, so a bank called KHE Amps in a set called User 1 reads User 1, KHE Amps.
  - New: OBS on the keys, over obs-websocket. Start and stop recording with a lamp that follows what OBS reports rather than what the key asked for, pause, chapter marks, and scene switching. A soft-key bank of kind OBS Scenes shows the scene names live with the one on air lit, and a marker named "obs: Wide" switches as the playhead passes it.
  - OBS scenes can be bound by name instead of by position, so reordering the scene list in OBS no longer repoints the keys silently. The old number still works.
  - Sticky Pot: a pin can carry a second parameter on the same pot, counter-running by default, which is how an 1176 is driven harder without the level moving. Both values are anchored when you pair them so nothing jumps, and moving either by hand afterwards is picked up from there. A pane of its own lists every pin in the project.
  - Fixed: letting go of the fader under FLIP wrote the focused parameter, or pan, instead of the pinned one. The release path was meant to mirror the live one and had every rung but that one.
  - Fixed: UF8 in a Send or Receive fader mode showed the level and the comp and gate GR of the track that would sit on the strip without the mode, while the name was the send's. All three now follow the send's destination or the receive's source, and a hardware output or an empty slot stays dark. The channel number follows it too. SEL and fader-touch select do nothing on a send strip and its lamp is dark, since selecting would change the track and empty the faders; Solo and Cut act on the send as before. The same for the UF1 as the Extender's ninth send strip, which also takes the send's colour now, like the UF8.
  - The Learn HUD's parameter list says where each parameter already sits: the slot on the UC1, the bank and strip on the UF8, the EXT FUNCS cells. Those cells are visible and assignable there too, with rename and clear.
  - AutoLearn moved into the HUD's parameter drawer: it proposes for the plug-in the HUD is showing, for the tab you are on, recognises a channel matrix, maps a plug-in that has no map, numbers EQ bands by their number, no longer matches Knee to Mix, refuses to write into a factory map, lists what it did not match, and stays on the plug-in you just mapped.
  - UF1: both footswitches are bindable, the preset browser owns its screen and reads SSL's own on-disk library for an SSL plug-in and REAPER's for everything else, opening on Shift + 5-8 in the Plugin view, four keys carry a binding per view, and Fades mode can show REAPER's crossfade editor while the edge you aim at is a crossfade.
  - Speed: the push-cycle menus and the FX-Learn parameter lists were rebuilding on every tick and every frame, which a plug-in with hundreds of parameters turned into a two-second wait after each click. Built once now, indexed rather than scanned, and written when the edits stop.
  - Windows: the combined FX-Learn layer is left Alt with left Ctrl.
  - Metering: gain reduction reads per strip on all eight UF8 strips, seven of which had been dark since April. Gate GR is there too, including the 32Classic's, and Combine GR composes with the source instead of being gated by it.
  - Fixed: FX Learn follows the plug-in the Learn HUD is on, and nothing else. Switching a map to "UF1 only" fills the UF1 layer first, a learned channel strip puts its soft-keys where a factory one has them, Create plus AutoLearn goes straight to the proposals, the listening run stops only at slots that have a UC1 control, UF1 pages turn by hand outside PLUGIN mode, and EXT FUNCS are learned by clicking the slot and wiggling the control.
  - New: a press on a surface selects that button in Settings, Bindings. Switchable under Behaviour, Bindings; the key that opens and closes Settings keeps working.
  - Fixed: with "Layers switch Quicks only" on, the Bindings pane shows the layer that fires instead of the layer that banks, so a binding no longer looks deleted while the key goes on firing it.
  - New: a long-press slot can repeat while the key is held. First shot at the half second as before, the rest at 20 to 1000 ms, 100 by default. Greyed out on an action that toggles.
  - New: REC steps a track's input channel without an RME interface. The input is REAPER's own; only preamp gain, 48V, pad and phase need TotalReaper.
  - Fixed: in REC + RME the value line belongs to the preamp on all three surfaces, and a hardware input without a preamp shows empty flags and "--dB" instead of pan on the UF1 or a stale reading on the UC1.
  - Fixed: a fresh REAPER never starts in UF8 Plug-in Mode, and a press the mode swallows flashes the banner.
  - Fixed: the banking window counts the strips that show a track, so DynaMount stands and Hue lamps no longer hide the tracks behind them.
  - Fixed: a failed surface reopen is retried every five seconds instead of once, so a UC1 that drops out comes back by itself.
  - Fixed: all three surfaces name the hardware input the REC keys are driving. The UC1 only flashed it for a second and a half after a channel change and then went back to naming the plug-in; it stands in the colour bar and in the model field now, from the same source as the UF8 and the UF1, and it repaints when the input changes.
  - Fixed: pointing a track from a channel with a preamp at one without left the old gain on the UC1, the one surface that does not rebuild its value line every tick.
  - Fixed: UF1 V-Pot push and UF1 Sends/Receives toggle could not be picked in Bindings. Both were bindable and sat in no category, and the picker drops a builtin whose category is empty, so the only way onto a key was to already have it on one. Hardware Modes and Sends / Receives now, and the check CI runs fails on any builtin the picker cannot show.
  - The bindings file moves to version 42. Every step is additive and a v0.5.9 setup loads unchanged.
